.Dd May 18, 2026
.Dt GROUPMOD 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm groupmod
.Nd modify an existing group
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl g Ar GID Op Fl o
.Op Fl n Ar NEW_NAME
.Ar GROUP
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
edits the
.Pa /etc/group
row for
.Ar GROUP
in place, with corresponding edits to
.Pa /etc/gshadow
(when present) and \(em on a GID change \(em to
.Pa /etc/passwd
so any user whose
.Va pw_gid
matched the old value is renumbered atomically.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl g Ar GID
Change the numeric GID.  Refuses an already-used GID unless
.Fl o
is given.
.It Fl o
With
.Fl g ,
allow non-unique GIDs.
.It Fl n Ar NEW_NAME
Rename the group.  Updates the group's own row in
.Pa /etc/group
and
.Pa /etc/gshadow ;
member-list references are
.Em not
rewritten because member lists name USERS, not groups.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
0 success, 2 bad usage, 3 bad value, 4 GID clash, 6 GROUP missing,
9 NEW_NAME in use, 10 database write failed.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr group 5 ,
.Xr gshadow 5 ,
.Xr groupadd 8 ,
.Xr groupdel 8 ,
.Xr usermod 8
.Sh AUTHORS
Substrate-native
.Nm ,
written to match the shadow-utils command-line surface.
